# Super+Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Q asks to log out: ⇧⌘Q on the Mac-first keyboard,
# which keyd hands on as exactly this. The question is the Ambrosia menu's
# Log Out…. It can be changed in System Settings, Shortcuts, like Search's.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Log Out
Comment=Ask to quit all apps and log out
Icon=system-log-out
Exec=/usr/bin/ambrosia log-out
NoDisplay=true
StartupNotify=false
X-KDE-Shortcuts=Meta+Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Q
